  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compare the variances of the two lotteries and prefer the one with lower variance (Lottery B). However, the individual did not consider variance at all. They did not mention any calculation, comparison, or evaluation of variability or spread. Their justification is based on subjective perception of risk being marginal and a general reluctance to choose either option. There is no alignment between the rule of the decision reason (comparing variance) and the individual’s reasoning (subjective risk perception and indecision). Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The final assessment is 0.",
